# model = dl07_MW_euv
# Size-integrated extinction, albedo and scattering asymmetry per H
# for the Draine & Li (2007) / Weingartner & Draine (2001) Milky-Way
# dust model.
#
# Model definition: WD01 R_V = 3.1, b_C = 6e-5 size distribution
#   (Draine's "MW 3.1_60"), with the Draine (2003a) x0.93 abundance
#   reduction applied, heated by the MMP83 field at U = 1 for the
#   PAH ionization fraction (WD01b charging).
# Size grid: Draine's 84-point log grid, 3.548 A - 5.012 um.
# Optics:
#   silicate     : Mie on the D03 astrosilicate dielectric function
#     ../data/dielectric/index_silD03
#   carbonaceous : absorption from the DL07 PAH <-> graphite xi-blend
#     (neutral and cation mixed by the ionization fraction, a > 100 A
#     fully ionized); scattering and <cos> from random-orientation D03
#     graphite (1/3 parallel + 2/3 perpendicular), which is the
#     standard DL07 treatment -- PAH scattering is Rayleigh-negligible.
#     ../data/dielectric/index_CpaD03, index_CpeD03
#
# Wavelength range:  6.205399E-05 -  3.981000E+04 um, 1761 points.
#   The floor is set by the D03 dielectric functions: the shorter-reaching
#   of silicate and graphite stops at  6.199200E-05 um, and a shorter floor is
#   refused because (n, k) would freeze at the boundary value there.
#
# How far to trust the EUV band of THIS model:
#   the optics are Mie on the D03 dielectric functions at EVERY
#   wavelength, so nothing changes character across the band, and the
#   result can be checked directly against Draine's own published
#   table kext_albedo_WD_MW_3.1_60_D03.all (2003 vintage), which
#   spans 1e-4 - 1e4 um.  Running this program prints that comparison
#   decade by decade.
#
# Column order follows Draine's kext_albedo tables and MoCHII's
#   par%ion_dust_kext reader: the first four columns are
#   lambda, albedo, <cos>, C_ext/H, and a reader may stop there.
#   Draine's 5th column is K_abs [cm^2/g]; ours is C_abs/H [cm^2/H],
#   so no dust-mass normalization is folded into these numbers.
#   A host running the Zubko model through an ionizing band needs
#   exactly such a file: that model has no EUV extension of its own
#   (its optics table IS the model definition), so the host reads the
#   ionizing-band optics from a curve file instead.
#
# SCOPE: these are size-integrated TRANSPORT optics, not a dust model.
#   There is no size-resolved Cabs(lambda, a), no grain enthalpy and no
#   Planck integral here, so stochastic heating and thermal emission
#   cannot be computed from this file.  A host that needs emission must
#   build the model (build_astrodust / build_dl07 / build_zubko /
#   build_from_files) and take these same curves from dust_extinction,
#   which keeps the absorbed power and the re-emitted spectrum
#   referring to one and the same grain.
#
# Units: lambda micron; cross sections cm^2 per H nucleon;
#   albedo and <cos> dimensionless.
#
#             lambda               albedo                <cos>              C_ext/H              C_abs/H              C_sca/H
#           (micron)                                                       (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/H)             (cm^2/H)
 6.205399200000E-005  7.081118809124E-001  9.999996615177E-001  4.604670533240E-025  1.344048620966E-025  3.260621912275E-025
 6.277419577535E-005  7.057895730341E-001  9.999996541811E-001  4.733701177665E-025  1.392704244610E-025  3.340996933055E-025
